---
// The whole architecture as a blueprint: every layer with its shape, the branch
// at h, and the one variable in the system (C, a repetition count, not a layer
// width). Static DOM; the structure is one fact.
---

<figure class="nbp">
	<div class="spine">
		<span class="lyr in"><b>the position</b><i>78 numbers</i></span>
		<span class="wire"><i>weights: 78 × 128</i></span>
		<span class="lyr"><b>trunk layer 1</b><i>128 activations</i></span>
		<span class="wire"><i>weights: 128 × 128</i></span>
		<span class="lyr h"><b>trunk layer 2</b><i>128 activations</i><em>this IS h, the summary. Not a separate part: the trunk's last layer.</em></span>
	</div>

	<div class="split">
		<div class="side">
			<span class="slbl">value head · runs once</span>
			<span class="wire"><i>weights: 128 × 64</i></span>
			<span class="lyr sm"><b>64 activations</b></span>
			<span class="wire"><i>weights: 64 × 1</i></span>
			<span class="lyr out"><b>1 number</b><i>how this game likely ends</i></span>
		</div>
		<div class="side">
			<span class="slbl">scorer · one pass over a stack of C rows</span>
			<span class="lyr cat stack">
				<span class="srow">h ∥ candidate 1</span>
				<span class="srow">h ∥ candidate 2</span>
				<span class="srow">h ∥ candidate 3</span>
				<i>⋮ one row per legal candidate: a matrix, C × (128 + a few dozen)</i>
			</span>
			<span class="wire"><i>weights: (128 + a few dozen) × 128, multiplied once against all C rows</i></span>
			<span class="lyr sm"><b>C × 128 activations</b></span>
			<span class="wire"><i>weights: 128 × 1, once again</i></span>
			<span class="lyr out"><b>C scores, one column</b><i>every candidate scored in the same two multiplies</i></span>
			<span class="soft">softmax over the column → a probability per legal move</span>
		</div>
	</div>

	<figcaption class="nbp-note">
		Every weight matrix above is a fixed shape; the same dials serve every question in
		the game. The only variable in the whole system is C, and C is not a layer width.
		It is a row count, and a matrix multiply handles ten rows exactly the way it
		handles one. A weight matrix never knows what a row means: in training, rows are
		different positions from the ledger; here, rows are different candidates.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.nbp {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
		padding: 1.2rem 1.2rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 14px;
	}
	.spine {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0;
		margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
	}
	.lyr {
		display: inline-flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		text-align: center;
		gap: 0.08rem;
		min-width: 220px;
		padding: 0.4em 0.9em;
		border: 2px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 9px;
		background: #fff;
	}
	.lyr b {
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}
	.lyr i {
		font-style: normal;
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	.lyr em {
		font-style: normal;
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		line-height: 1.3;
		color: var(--accent);
		max-width: 260px;
	}
	.lyr.in {
		border-style: dashed;
	}
	.lyr.h {
		border-color: var(--accent);
		background: #eef1ff;
	}
	.lyr.cat {
		border-color: var(--accent);
		border-style: dashed;
		background: #eef1ff;
	}
	.lyr.stack {
		gap: 0.2rem;
		padding-top: 0.55em;
	}
	.srow {
		display: block;
		width: 200px;
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		padding: 0.14em 0;
		border: 1.5px solid var(--accent);
		border-radius: 5px;
		background: #fff;
	}
	.lyr.sm {
		min-width: 160px;
	}
	.lyr.out {
		border-color: #177a4c;
		background: #eaf4ee;
	}
	.side:last-child .lyr.out {
		border-color: #b4341f;
		background: #faf1ee;
	}
	.wire {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.1rem 0;
	}
	.wire::before,
	.wire::after {
		content: "";
		width: 2px;
		height: 7px;
		background: rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.wire i {
		font-style: normal;
		font-size: 0.66rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		padding: 0.05rem 0.4rem;
	}
	.split {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: start;
		padding-top: 0.8rem;
		border-top: 1px dashed rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.side {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
	}
	.slbl {
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.soft {
		margin-top: 0.45rem;
		font-size: 0.74rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		text-align: center;
	}
	.nbp-note {
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
		padding-top: 0.6rem;
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.split {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
